msgid "Filters"
msgstr "Filtros"

# CTX-INTERPRETATION: This string appears in a tour guide, explaining how to
# use filters to organize a dashboard, specifying filtering by shared
# resources and assigned tags.
#: services/static-webserver/client/source/resource/osparc/tours/tiplite_tours.json:58
#: services/static-webserver/client/source/resource/osparc/tours/tis_tours.json:77
msgid ""
"These filters allows you to display a better organized Dashboard.<br>You can"
" filter by with with whom the resources is Shared with and also Tags if you "
"assign them."
msgstr ""
"Estos filtros le permiten mostrar un panel de control más organizado. Puede "
"filtrar por con quién se comparten los recursos y también por las etiquetas "
"que haya asignado."

# CTX-INTERPRETATION: The string "Filters and Search" appears in the context
# of a user interface element, likely a button or heading, that provides
# access to filtering and search functionality within a scientific simulation
# application, possibly related to plans or studies.
#: services/static-webserver/client/source/resource/osparc/tours/tiplite_tours.json:62
#: services/static-webserver/client/source/resource/osparc/tours/tis_tours.json:81
msgid "Filters and Search"
msgstr "Filtros y Búsqueda"

# CTX-INTERPRETATION: This string appears in a tour guide, explaining how to
# use the search and filter functionality within the application.
#: services/static-webserver/client/source/resource/osparc/tours/tiplite_tours.json:63
#: services/static-webserver/client/source/resource/osparc/tours/tis_tours.json:82
msgid ""
"This tool allows you to search and filter Plans.<br>You can search and "
"filter by:<br>- Title, description, owner, id...<br>- Tags<br>- Shared with"
msgstr ""
"Esta herramienta le permite buscar y filtrar Planes.<br>Puede buscar y "
"filtrar por:<br>- Título, descripción, propietario, id...<br>- "
"Etiquetas<br>- Compartido con"

# CTX-INTERPRETATION: This string appears within a tour guide, explaining how
# to access additional options related to a 'Plan' card, likely within a user
# interface.
#: services/static-webserver/client/source/resource/osparc/tours/tiplite_tours.json:72
#: services/static-webserver/client/source/resource/osparc/tours/tis_tours.json:91
msgid ""
"On the Plan card, you can use the three dots button to access more "
"information and operation on the Plan."
msgstr ""
"En la tarjeta 'Plan', puede usar el botón de tres puntos para acceder a más "
"información y operaciones relacionadas con la Plan."

# CTX-INTERPRETATION: This string appears within a tour guide, explaining how
# to update a service on the Plan card using the Update button.
#: services/static-webserver/client/source/resource/osparc/tours/tiplite_tours.json:77
#: services/static-webserver/client/source/resource/osparc/tours/tis_tours.json:96
msgid ""
"On the Plan card, you can use the Update button to update the corresponding "
"service to its latest version."
msgstr ""
"En la tarjeta 'Plan', puede usar el botón 'Update' para actualizar el "
"servicio correspondiente a la última versión."

# CTX-INTERPRETATION: This string appears within a tour guide, explaining the
# 'Activity Center' feature, which allows users to monitor running
# simulations, recent activity, and completed tasks.
#: services/static-webserver/client/source/resource/osparc/tours/tis_tours.json:10
msgid ""
"Here you can track all your running simulations, recent activity, and "
"completed tasks. If you want to check the results once these are ready, you "
"will find more details in the Activity Overview on the Project card."
msgstr ""
"Aquí puede realizar un seguimiento de todas sus simulaciones en ejecución, "
"la actividad reciente y las tareas completadas. Si desea consultar los "
"resultados una vez que estén disponibles, encontrará más detalles en la "
"Vista de Actividad en la tarjeta del Proyecto."

# CTX-INTERPRETATION: The string "Personalized Plans" appears within a JSON
# file describing a guided tour related to purchasing credits for personalized
# simulations in the Osparc application.
#: services/static-webserver/client/source/resource/osparc/tours/tis_tours.json:62
msgid "Personalized Plans"
msgstr "Planes Personalizados"

# CTX-INTERPRETATION: This string describes personalized simulation plans,
# highlighting their features and associated costs, and directs users to a
# 'Buy Credits' guided tour.
#: services/static-webserver/client/source/resource/osparc/tours/tis_tours.json:63
msgid ""
"These plans support personalization and allow for customized models. Running"
" the simulations required for personalized optimization will incur charges. "
"Choose these plans for advanced stimulation optimization. If you want to "
"learn how to purchase credits, follow the 'Buy Credits' Guided Tour."
msgstr ""
"Estos planes admiten la personalización y permiten modelos personalizados. "
"Ejecutar las simulaciones necesarias para la optimización personalizada "
"conllevará cargos. Elija estos planes para una optimización avanzada. Si "
"desea aprender a comprar créditos, siga el 'Tour de Compra de Créditos'."

# CTX-INTERPRETATION: The string appears in the TI tours section, explaining
# the need for credits to run personalized plans and guiding the user to
# purchase them.
#: services/static-webserver/client/source/resource/osparc/tours/tis_tours.json:103
msgid "Buy Credits for Personalization"
msgstr "Comprar Créditos para Personalización"

# CTX-INTERPRETATION: The string appears within a tour guide for personalized
# TI plans, explaining the need for credits and how to acquire them.
#: services/static-webserver/client/source/resource/osparc/tours/tis_tours.json:107
msgid ""
"In order to run personalized TI plans, Credits are required. In the next "
"steps you will learn how to purchase them."
msgstr ""
"Para poder ejecutar planes TI personalizados, se requieren Créditos. En los "
"siguientes pasos, aprenderá cómo adquirirlos."

# CTX-INTERPRETATION: This string appears within a JSON file defining tour
# elements for a user interface, specifically related to credit accounts and
# access permissions.
#: services/static-webserver/client/source/resource/osparc/tours/tis_tours.json:124
msgid ""
"This lists the Credit Accounts you have access to. Apart from your own "
"Account, the list also includes Credit Accounts that were shared with you."
msgstr ""
"Esta sección enumera las cuentas de crédito a las que tiene acceso. Además "
"de su propia cuenta, la lista también incluye las cuentas de crédito que se "
"le han compartido."

# CTX-INTERPRETATION: This string appears within a tour guide, explaining how
# to add credits to a user's account, offering options for auto-top-up or one-
# time payments.
#: services/static-webserver/client/source/resource/osparc/tours/tis_tours.json:129
msgid ""
"There are two ways to add Credits to your Credit Account: you can set up an "
"auto-top-up procedure or make a one-time payment."
msgstr ""
"Hay dos formas de agregar Créditos a su Cuenta de Créditos: puede configurar"
" un procedimiento de recarga automática o realizar un pago único."

# CTX-INTERPRETATION: The string "Auto-Recharge" appears as the title of a
# feature explaining automatic credit replenishment, requiring a payment
# method to be set up first.
#: services/static-webserver/client/source/resource/osparc/tours/tis_tours.json:133
msgid "Auto-Recharge"
msgstr "Re carga automática"

# CTX-INTERPRETATION: This string appears in a tour guide, explaining the
# automated credit top-up feature and the requirement to add a payment method
# before it can be used.
#: services/static-webserver/client/source/resource/osparc/tours/tis_tours.json:134
msgid ""
"Keep your balance running smoothly by automatically setting your Credits to "
"be topped up when it runs low. Before the automated top-up function can be "
"activated, you must add a payment method."
msgstr ""
"Mantenga su saldo funcionando sin problemas configurando automáticamente que"
" sus Créditos se reabastezcan cuando se agoten. Antes de que pueda activarse"
" la función de recarga automática, debe agregar un método de pago."

# CTX-INTERPRETATION: The string "One-Time payment" appears in a tour guide,
# explaining how users can add credits to their account with a single payment.
#: services/static-webserver/client/source/resource/osparc/tours/tis_tours.json:138
msgid "One-Time payment"
msgstr "Pago único"

# CTX-INTERPRETATION: This string appears within a tour guide, explaining how
# users can add credits to their account using a one-time payment and save the
# payment method for future use.
#: services/static-webserver/client/source/resource/osparc/tours/tis_tours.json:139
msgid ""
"You can top up your Credits with a one-off, non-recurring payment. After the"
" payment is made, the new Credits will be added to your Credit Account. The "
"payment method can be saved for future top ups."
msgstr ""
"Puede rellenar sus Créditos con un pago único e intransferible. Después de "
"realizar el pago, los nuevos Créditos se añadirán a su Cuenta de Créditos. "
"El método de pago puede guardarse para futuros recargos."

# CTX-INTERPRETATION: This string appears within a JSON file defining tour
# instructions, likely informing the user about the status of their payment
# and credit availability.
#: services/static-webserver/client/source/resource/osparc/tours/tis_tours.json:146
msgid ""
"Once the payment is validated, the Credits will be added to your Credit "
"Account and they will be ready to be used."
msgstr ""
"Una vez que el pago se haya validado, los Créditos se agregarán a su Cuenta "
"de Créditos y estarán listos para ser utilizados."
